From: Impre-visible <69050895+Impre-visible@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:47:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] GPU: VICTORY_CARD_AWAKE=idle keeps the card awake only
 while our queue has nothing to run (off by default)

VICTORY_CARD_AWAKE=1 keeps a 64-thread count of about 2 ms running on a
compute queue for as long as submissions go out, two on the way at a time,
to hold the clocks up over the short idle stretches between submissions. On
a card that is busy the whole frame it has nothing to do: run z3a (GTX 1660,
Series S) had the card idle 2-6 ms a frame by the card clock, and there the
count only shares the card with the frame's own work, on a second queue.

With VICTORY_CARD_AWAKE=idle the count is sent only while the card clock
says the drawing queue has run everything of ours sent to it (the clock's
watching thread marks the idle stretch, Host::card_sent ends it), is about
a quarter of a millisecond long, and one is on the way at a time (looked at
every quarter millisecond while not wanted): a submission sent meanwhile
waits a quarter of a millisecond at most. =1, =turns and unset are as
before. What is drawn is the same in every mode.

A/B in one run: VICTORY_CARD_AWAKE=turns (20 s on, 20 s off, the log says
when) shows what =1 costs or gains on this card; then =idle against =1 and
against unset, same scene, ms/frame and "on the GPU".

